  /Alt (This table presents an excerpt from the EAGLE (EIONET Action Group on Land monitoring in Europe) matrix, detailing hierarchical classifications for Land Cover Components (LCC) and Land Use Attributes (LUA) used within the Copernicus Land Monitoring Service (CLMS) CLC+ Core consortium. The table includes the following metadata fields: `Class Code*` with value `84100`, `Name*` with value `Open sea`, `100% EAGLE Compliant*` with value `Yes`, and `Colour Code` with value `#e6f5f3`. / Code / Label / Level / Factor / /---/---/---/---/ / LCC-2_2_1_2 / Reeds, Bamboos, Canes / 4 / / / LCC-2_2_2 / Non-Graminoids (Forbs, Ferns) / 3 / / / LCC-2_3 / Succulents, Cacti / 2 / / / LCC-2_4 / Lichens, Mosses, Algae / 2 / / / LCC-2_4_1 / Lichens / 3 / / / LCC-2_4_2 / Mosses / 3 / / / LCC-2_4_3 / Algae / 3 / / / LCC-2_4_3_1 / Macro Algae / 4 / / / LCC-2_4_3_2 / Micro Algae (Plankton) / 4 / / / LCC-3 / Water / 1 / / / LCC-3_1 / Liquid Water Bodies / 2 / / / LCC-3_1_1 / Inland Water Bodies / 3 / / / LCC-3_1_1_1 / Water Course / 4 / / / LCC-3_1_1_2 / Standing Water / 4 / / / LCC-3_1_2 / Marine Waters / 3 / 5 / / LCC-3_2 / Solid Waters / 2 / / / LCC-3_2_1 / Snow / 3 / / / LCC-3_2_2 / Ice, Glaciers / 3 / / / LUA / Land Use Attributes / 0 / / / LUA-1 / Primary Production Sector / 1 / / / LUA-1_1 / Agriculture / 2 / / / LUA-1_1_1 / Commercial Crop Production / 3 / / / LUA-1_1_2 / Farming Infrastructure / 3 / / / LUA-1_1_2_1 / Animal Husbandry / 4 / / / LUA-1_1_2_2 / Farming Storage / 4 / / / LUA-1_1_2_3 / Other Farming Infrastructure / 4 / / / LUA-1_1_3 / Production for Own Consumption / 3 / / / LUA-1_2 / Forestry / 2 / / / LUA-1_3 / Mining and Quarrying / 2 / / / LUA-1_4 / Aquaculture and Fishing / 2 / / / LUA-1_4_1 / Aquaculture / 3 / / / LUA-1_4_2 / Professional Wild Fishery / 3 / / / LUA-1_5 / Other Primary Production / 2 / / / LUA-1_5_1 / Hunting / 3 / / / LUA-1_5_2 / Migratory Animals / 3 / / / LUA-1_5_3 / Picking Natural Products / 3 / / / LUA-1_5_4 / Apiculture (Bee Hives) / 3 / / The table details Land Cover Components (LCC) such as vegetation (e.g., Reeds, Bamboos, Canes, Lichens, Mosses, Algae) and various water bodies (e.g., Inland Water Bodies, Standing Water, Marine Waters, Snow, Ice, Glaciers), alongside Land Use Attributes (LUA) related to primary production (e.g., Agriculture, Forestry, Mining and Quarrying, Aquaculture and Fishing). Each entry includes a hierarchical `Code`, `Label`, and `Level` (ranging from 0 for broad categories like LUA to 4 for highly specific types like Micro Algae or Animal Husbandry), with only `Marine Waters` having a `Factor` of `5`.)
  /A [<<
    /O /Layout
    /Placement /Block
  >>]
  /K [0]
  /Pg 4392 0 R
>>
endobj

